{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,280p' /app/agent-output/S11-mermaid-lazyload-trap/report.md; git -C /app status --short -- /app/fixture /app/agent-output 2>/dev/null || true\"","aggregated_output":"# S11 — Mermaid lazy-load trap\n\n## 1. Split-chunk failure\n\nThe first request succeeded, but that only fetched the entry module. The bundled\n`mermaid-chunk.js` still contained relative imports for Mermaid's other generated\nmodules. The browser resolved those specifiers relative to the resource URL and\nrequested `src-BfvxrPJe.js`, `pie-WAS4IAKB-CQHCQWWM.js`, and the other siblings.\nThose files were not in the shipped `lib/`, so the requests returned 404 and\nevaluation of the entry import rejected with `Failed to fetch dynamically imported\nmodule`. The fallback was therefore expected.\n\nThe build must either ship the entire emitted module graph at the same relative\nURLs, or, for this plugin's resource, build the lazy entry as one self-contained\nbundle (`bundle: true`, with code splitting/splitting disabled). The latter keeps\nthe initial Mermaid load lazy while removing the unshipped sibling dependency.\n\n## 2. Windows 403\n\nThe flawed check is the string-prefix check after `realpathSync`:\n\n```ts\nfile = normalize(realpathSync(abs))\nif (!file.startsWith(LIB_DIR + sep)) reject()\n```\n\n`fileURLToPath(new URL('.', import.meta.url))` returns a native filesystem path\nusing the drive-letter spelling in the file URL/path used to initialize the\nplugin. `normalize` performs lexical separator and dot cleanup; it does not\ncanonicalize case. Thus the production value of `LIB_DIR` starts with `E:`.\n\n`realpathSync(abs)` resolves the filesystem path and, on that Windows host,\nreturns the same location with a lowercase drive prefix, `e:`. The second\n`normalize` does not change that case. JavaScript `String.prototype.startsWith`\nis an exact, case-sensitive string comparison, so `e:\\\\dsh\\\\...` does not start\nwith `E:\\\\dsh\\\\...`, even though Windows filesystem resolution treats them as\nthe same drive/path. The evidence shows exactly this pair of values. Linux has\nno drive-letter case change and its absolute path spelling remains consistent,\nso the comparison passes there; the C: machines passed only because their\nspellings happened to line up.\n\n## 3. Guard and serving fix\n\nCompare paths with the platform-aware path operation `relative`, after\ncanonicalizing both sides, rather than comparing strings. For example:\n\n```ts\nconst root = normalize(realpathSync(LIB_DIR))\nconst file = normalize(realpathSync(abs))\nconst fromRoot = relative(root, file)\nconst outside = isAbsolute(fromRoot) ||\n  fromRoot === '..' || fromRoot.startsWith('..' + sep)\nif (outside) reject()\n```\n\n(`root` can be computed once at route setup.) `path.relative` uses Windows path\nsemantics, including its case-insensitive drive comparison, while on POSIX it\nkeeps the required case-sensitive semantics. Checking for `..` as a complete\nsegment also avoids the usual prefix mistake such as accepting `lib2` as a\nchild of `lib`. Canonicalizing the candidate with `realpathSync` before this\ncheck preserves the protection against a symlink escaping the plugin directory.\n\nA dynamic import also requires every requested module URL to be actually\nfetchable: the route must return the exact JavaScript file with a successful\nresponse and a JavaScript MIME type (for example, `200` and\n`application/javascript`). If splitting is retained, that requirement applies\nto every sibling chunk too, not only `mermaid-chunk.js`.\n\n## 4. Ctrl+scroll ownership\n\nThe wheel event originates in the diagram in the modal and bubbles through its\nancestors, so both the modal zoom handler and the pane font-size handler can\nobserve it. `preventDefault()` only suppresses the browser's native default\naction; it does not stop another JavaScript listener. Likewise, propagation and\nlistener placement matter: `stopPropagation()` does not prevent another\nlistener on the same `EventTarget`, and registration order can make either\nhandler run first.\n\nThe ownership rule should be explicit: the nearest active surface owns the\nevent. While the modal is open, a Ctrl+wheel whose composed path is inside the\nmodal belongs exclusively to the modal. The modal handles zoom and prevents the\nnative default; the pane handler must return for that target/state. If both\nhandlers are necessarily on the same target, use the ownership gate (or\n`stopImmediatePropagation()` where appropriate), rather than relying on\nlistener registration order. When the modal is closed, the pane may own the\nevent.\n\n## 5. Regression coverage\n\n1. **Bundle graph test (incident 1).** Build the Mermaid lazy entry in release\n   mode, inspect the publish artifact, and assert that either the entry has no\n   unresolved relative chunk imports or every referenced sibling exists under\n   the shipped `lib/` path. Serve only the package artifact and load at least a\n   pie diagram through the real resource URL; fail on any 404 or rejected module\n   import.\n\n2. **Route containment matrix (incident 2).** Exercise an in-root file where the\n   configured Windows root is `E:\\\\...` but canonical `realpathSync` returns\n   `e:\\\\...`; it must return 200. Run the same test on Windows and POSIX, and\n   include `..`, a sibling such as `lib2`, and an in-root symlink to an outside\n   file, which must be rejected. This directly tests the path API behavior that\n   the old `startsWith` guard missed.\n\n3. **Modal wheel ownership test (incident 3).** Dispatch a bubbling, cancelable\n   Ctrl+wheel targeted at a diagram inside an open modal and assert exactly one\n   zoom action, zero pane font-size actions, and the intended cancellation.\n   Repeat with the modal closed and expect the pane action instead. Register the\n   listeners in both orders (or run the browser integration test with both\n   placements) to ensure ownership, not event-listener ordering, determines the\n   result.\n\n?? agent-output/\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
